# Linear Regression from Scratch

A hands-on implementation of **Linear Regression from scratch using Python and NumPy**, built to understand the mathematics and optimization process behind linear regression rather than relying on libraries such as Scikit-learn.

The model is trained on a salary dataset, using **Years of Experience** as the input feature and **Salary** as the target variable.

## 📌 Project Overview

This project explores how a simple linear regression model can learn the relationship between an employee's years of experience and their salary.

The dataset is loaded using Pandas:

```python
ds = pd.read_csv("Linear_Regre_Scratch/Salary_Data.csv")

X = ds["YearsExperience"].values
Y = ds["Salary"].values
```

The implementation then trains a custom regression model using gradient-based optimization and records the loss throughout training.

